WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.127
- [Announcer 1:] He's been
slow in the last few weeks

00:00:02.127 --> 00:00:04.129
going into the shutdown.

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:06.965
That must be the confidence.
How about that?

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:08.508
- [Announcer 2:] That started with
a breakup

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:09.342
of a pass, Brez.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.094
- During the game, after LeBron dunked,

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:15.432
he either said, “I'm still
the baddest out here”

00:00:15.432 --> 00:00:17.267
or “I'm still the fastest out here.”

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.689
OK, I asked LeBron if he said

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:26.234
that he was still the
baddest or still the fastest.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:29.154
He looked at me and said,
“What do you think I said?”

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:31.698
- [Flight attendant:] Welcome to Orlando.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.491
The local time is 10:33.

00:00:34.617 --> 00:00:35.660
- Most importantly,

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.787
always have to start the day with a mask.

00:00:39.122 --> 00:00:41.541
[Funky music]

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.795
On the way to practice No. 1.

00:00:45.795 --> 00:00:48.715
[Funky music]

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:51.342
OK, so right now we are
in the Wide World of Sports

00:00:51.342 --> 00:00:53.053
on the northwest side, getting ready

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.345
to go to Rockets practice.

00:00:54.345 --> 00:00:56.306
It's the first practice
that we are going to.

00:00:56.306 --> 00:00:57.807
Teams are staggered throughout the day

00:00:57.807 --> 00:00:59.309
in different locations, but

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:01.186
Rockets are right now.

00:01:01.186 --> 00:01:03.063
- Thank you, Austin.
- Good job, Tracy.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:06.066
[Laughing]

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:07.358
- We gotta practice, bro.

00:01:07.358 --> 00:01:08.693
- Bro, ask him, bro.

00:01:08.693 --> 00:01:10.820
He the one that got all
the fuckin’ questions.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:12.572
Yeah, he the one that got all the questions.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:15.492
- One question.
- [Austin Rivers:] Goddamn.

00:01:15.492 --> 00:01:18.369
- Heading to practice No. 2.

00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:20.330
Going to watch the Miami Heat.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.791
- What time is it?
Aw, yeah, it's Mickey time.

00:01:22.791 --> 00:01:25.210
[Funky music]

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:26.336
Hold on. Don't get me right now.

00:01:26.336 --> 00:01:27.170
My mask not up.
- [Taylor laughing]

00:01:28.463 --> 00:01:29.464
- Where we going?

00:01:29.464 --> 00:01:30.298
How are you, Taylor?

00:01:30.298 --> 00:01:31.132
- I'm fantastic.
- You good?

00:01:31.132 --> 00:01:32.842
- [Taylor:] So you said
that it was gonna be TBD

00:01:32.842 --> 00:01:35.261
what you do with your jersey.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.472
What was the feeling when it was rejected?

00:01:38.848 --> 00:01:40.308
- I mean, we can't say that

00:01:41.392 --> 00:01:44.395
I didn't think that it would be a problem.

00:01:44.395 --> 00:01:45.772
But, like I said,

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.732
I'm hoping that they come
back and see the message

00:01:47.732 --> 00:01:49.651
that I want to get out there

00:01:49.651 --> 00:01:51.319
and let me speak on something

00:01:51.319 --> 00:01:53.404
the way that I would
like to speak on it.

00:01:53.404 --> 00:01:55.031
Like I said, to be determined.

00:01:55.031 --> 00:01:57.158
We really don't know. I'll
keep pressing for it.

00:01:57.158 --> 00:01:59.119
And I hear plenty of other
players around the league

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.995
would like to do the same, so

00:02:00.995 --> 00:02:03.414
I just, I hope that they see the message

00:02:03.414 --> 00:02:04.958
that we want to get across

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.168
and they let us be who we are.

00:02:07.168 --> 00:02:10.505
Get your ass from
behind the damn screen.

00:02:10.505 --> 00:02:13.258
Dunc. Dunc.
- Yo.

00:02:13.258 --> 00:02:15.885
- Duncan’s here, ready to go!

00:02:15.885 --> 00:02:18.346
- So we know you are big into fashion.

00:02:18.346 --> 00:02:21.141
How has that changed in
Orlando or has it changed?

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:23.351
- I brought everything with me, so

00:02:23.351 --> 00:02:25.436
I got enough options ready

00:02:25.436 --> 00:02:27.063
to have something every day.

00:02:27.063 --> 00:02:29.732
- Okay, Tuesday, July 21,

00:02:29.732 --> 00:02:31.651
very busy day.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:34.070
We're headed to Blazers practice first.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:36.489
[Funky music]

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:48.668
Portland wins the award for best DJ.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:49.502
Best DJ.

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.922
[Hip-hop music]

00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:04.767
Lakers practice second.

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:07.187
[Funky music]

00:03:09.272 --> 00:03:11.024
So, we know obviously
you're focused on winning,

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:12.859
but we heard Vogel talk about why

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:15.111
you should be Defensive
Player of the Year.

00:03:15.111 --> 00:03:16.404
What were your thoughts on what he said,

00:03:16.404 --> 00:03:18.072
and what's your case?

00:03:18.072 --> 00:03:19.908
- I didn't hear what was said.

00:03:19.908 --> 00:03:21.034
What was that?

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:22.827
- Well, what's your case
for why you should get it?

00:03:22.827 --> 00:03:24.454
- I don't have a case. I'll let that—

00:03:24.454 --> 00:03:28.374
I’ll let my teammates decide
and the fans decide. But

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:32.503
I just go out there and play
hard every night, you know?

00:03:32.503 --> 00:03:35.590
My biggest impact that I
think I have is defensively.

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:39.135
I love playing defense. I
love stopping other players,

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.846
making it tough on other players. So,

00:03:43.306 --> 00:03:45.350
that’s just like my case in a nutshell.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:47.435
- And we end the day with
the Celtics practice.

00:03:47.435 --> 00:03:49.854
[Funky music]

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.068
- Get that shit outta here!

00:04:00.782 --> 00:04:02.742
- Ah, fuckin' hate you.

00:04:03.952 --> 00:04:05.119
- Hey, hey, hey!

00:04:06.162 --> 00:04:07.080
- [Taylor:] There we go.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.915
Man, oh, man.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.416
I am exhausted.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:11.876
Best parts of today:

00:04:11.876 --> 00:04:14.587
The Lakers ended their pre-practice huddle

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:18.174
putting hands in and
saying, "One, two, three, Mamba."

00:04:19.384 --> 00:04:20.969
That was a really nice,

00:04:20.969 --> 00:04:22.929
really, really touching moment.

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:25.014
That was my favorite part of the day.

00:04:25.014 --> 00:04:27.225
I think I'm gonna end on that.

00:04:27.225 --> 00:04:30.436
This is the first day of
actual basketball play.

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:33.189
Obviously not a game, but a
scrimmage for competition!

00:04:33.189 --> 00:04:35.024
Teams facing one another.

00:04:35.024 --> 00:04:36.025
I'm looking forward to it, so

00:04:36.025 --> 00:04:38.736
I'm heading to the arena right now.

00:04:38.736 --> 00:04:41.823
[Laid-back music]

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:49.622
- [Taylor:] On a scale of one to 10,

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:52.417
10 being the most different,

00:04:52.417 --> 00:04:54.502
how would you rate playing again?

00:04:54.502 --> 00:04:55.628
- An 11.

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:57.505
That was different. You know,

00:04:57.505 --> 00:04:58.673
when you come out for warm-ups

00:04:58.673 --> 00:05:00.633
and, like, literally no one is out there,

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:04.262
and I went over to some of the referees,

00:05:04.262 --> 00:05:08.141
talked to Leon and Scott
a little bit beforehand.

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:10.685
And even then, they were like,

00:05:10.685 --> 00:05:12.729
“This is just surreal.”

00:05:12.729 --> 00:05:15.815
[Funky music]

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.443
- All right, it's Thursday, July 23.

00:05:18.443 --> 00:05:20.153
I'm getting ready, as you can see.

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:22.780
Very big day, second day of scrimmages,

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:25.283
I'll be at Bucks-Spurs at 3:00,

00:05:25.283 --> 00:05:27.702
then I'll be at Lakers-Mavs at 7:00.

00:05:27.702 --> 00:05:28.536
- Hut hut!

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:35.668
- OK, OK.

00:05:38.546 --> 00:05:40.298
My man, do that.

00:05:40.298 --> 00:05:42.675
- So today, Becky Hammon is the head coach.

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:44.677
I'm loving it. It's definitely
my favorite thing

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:46.346
that I've seen so far in Orlando.

00:05:47.221 --> 00:05:49.140
She has complete control of the team.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:52.727
The guys are listening. They’re soaking
in everything she's saying.

00:05:52.727 --> 00:05:53.561
It's great.

00:05:53.561 --> 00:05:56.189
Hey, Becky. So once these
scrimmages are over,

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:57.815
what will success look like for you?

00:05:57.815 --> 00:05:59.734
Meaning, what will you
have to see to say, “OK,

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:02.070
we got better. These served their purpose”?

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:04.197
- Well, we gotta get better on
the defensive side of the ball.

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:05.948
It's been a struggle for us all year.

00:06:05.948 --> 00:06:08.076
We've been poor in transition,

00:06:08.076 --> 00:06:10.161
and we've been poor in
the half-court defense.

00:06:10.161 --> 00:06:11.204
We gotta get better rim protection.

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:12.455
I mean, you could go down the list.

00:06:12.455 --> 00:06:13.748
There's a litany of things

00:06:13.748 --> 00:06:16.000
that we could do better defensively,

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.002
and I think that's the big growth piece.

00:06:19.128 --> 00:06:20.421
- [Taylor:] The cleaning crew.

00:06:21.839 --> 00:06:23.633
We washed our hands, but

00:06:23.633 --> 00:06:26.135
there's a door, and
obviously we can't touch it

00:06:26.135 --> 00:06:27.512
because, you know, COVID-19,

